  "worked_solution": "The law that disjunction absorbs conjunction is stated as\n\n$$\nL\u2228(L\u2227\u00acM)\u2261L.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is logically equivalent to $L.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\u2228(\u00acM\u2227L) & \u2261L\u2228(L\u2227\u00acM) \\\\  & \u2261L.\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is logically equivalent to $L.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(L\u2227\u00acM)\u2228L & \u2261L\u2228(L\u2227\u00acM) \\\\  & \u2261L.\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is logically equivalent to $L.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\u00acM\u2227L)\u2228L & \u2261L\u2228(\u00acM\u2227L) \\\\  & \u2261L\u2228(L\u2227\u00acM) \\\\  & \u2261L.\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"",
